  "latestMilestone": "Canonical SWIR_OS main now includes verified safe same-user controls in the native GTK4 Task Manager/System Monitor. The process list supports bounded PID/name filtering and explicit selection; End Process requires confirmation and sends SIGTERM only to a process owned by the signed-in user after PID, UID, process name and /proc start-time identity are revalidated to reject PID reuse. PID 1, the monitor itself and the ancestor/session chain are protected; pidfd signaling is preferred where available, with no SIGKILL, sudo, pkexec, process-group kill or privilege elevation. Dedicated policy/self-test, real disposable-child SIGTERM, Wayland and Debian 13 gates plus the post-merge System Edition, Diagnostics and Core Apps gates are green. The authoritative roadmap intentionally remains 55/65 (84.6%) because the broader essential native daily-use application suite is still incomplete. Physical Live USB qualification remains pending; Secure Boot and legacy BIOS are not claimed.",
